Subject: [PATCH] 3895: the helper's card names the person to meet as the
 helper saved them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 58347, 0 of 3: Levan saved the target as „ბექუნა ფოტოგრაფი";
the owner typed „ბექა მაისურაძე", the target's registered name. Levan's
card said „ბექა მაისურაძეს" every time, for two reasons:

- the owner's words are not in Levan's label, so the name match in his
  book found nobody, and the request carries no number;
- the name read for a number (nameInBridgeBook) prefers the REGISTERED
  name to the label, so even a found number would have given the same.

targetNameForMediator now finds the number also as exactly one of the
mediator's contacts registered under that very name, and reads the
mediator's OWN label for it. The push to the mediator names the target
the same way. Anything unclear still keeps the asker's name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
